hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27637","Haddathana Waki': Haddathana al-A'mash, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd al-Fa'ishi, from a daughter of Khabbab, she said: Khabbab went out in an expedition, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would look after us, even milking a goat of ours. She said: He would milk it until it overflowed or poured forth, then when Khabbab returned he milked it and its yield returned to what it was. So we said to him: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to milk it until it poured forth, and he said once: until it filled, then when you milked it, its yield returned."
"27638","Haddathana Khalaf ibn al-Walid, he said: Haddathana Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Malik al-Ahmasi, from a daughter of Khabbab ibn al-Aratt, she said: My father went out in a battle and left nothing except a sheep, and she mentioned similar to it."
